      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Service Integrations**\n\nI'm now focusing on service integrations for this OCR/layout extraction task. Having reviewed `extract_text.py`, I see it leverages `azure.ai.documentintelligence`. Consequently, I'm leaning toward employing Azure Document Intelligence for similar files, specifically `extract_layout`. This seems like a consistent and logical path forward for seamless integration.\n\n\n**Defining Service Structure**\n\nI've outlined the architecture for the service integrations. I'll create `document_client.py` and `document_models.py` as Azure Document Intelligence helpers. The plan is now to build `extract_layout.py`, `extract_tables.py`, and `extract_key_values.py` using Azure's services, maintaining consistency. I'll then tackle the Google Cloud integrations, for the later steps, with `ocr_translate.py` using the Translation API and `ocr_safety.py` leveraging Vertex AI.\n\n\n**Outlining Module Creation**\n\nI'm now diving into the implementation phase. I've broken down the necessary files: `document_client.py` for Azure client utilities, and `document_models.py` for request/response models. I will create `extract_layout.py`, `extract_tables.py`, and `extract_key_values.py` using Azure. I will then work on Google Cloud integrations: `ocr_translate.py`, `ocr_safety.py`, `document_field_extraction.py` and `ocr_embedding.py`. Starting with `document_client.py`.\n\n\n",
